1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
In this video, we're going to show you how you can integrate Burp Suite Enterprise Edition with GitLab.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Once the integration is complete, you'll be able to raise GitLab issues directly from Burp for vulnerabilities that are found by your scans.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Now before you start, you'll need to make sure that you have access to Burp as an administrator,

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
you have access to your GitLab instance as an administrator,

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:33,000
and that you're also either the maintainer or the owner for the GitLab projects which you want to create issues on.

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,000
The first thing we're going to do is we're going to generate a GitLab impersonation token.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
GitLab have recently changed how their access tokens are generated,

8
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,000
and as a consequence, the token exceeds our character limit for access tokens.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
You can use the following workaround to get around this.

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
If you go to the URL that's shown on the screen,

11
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:57,000
you can remove the personal access token prefix from the GitLab configuration and then save the changes.

12
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,000
This should shrink the GitLab access token down to the required length.

13
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Once you've done this, you can then generate the impersonation token.

14
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
To do this, you should go to GitLab and then go to the admin area.

15
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:13,000
In here, we should select the user which you want Burp to use to raise the GitLab issues.

16
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:20,000
To do this, I'm going to go to users, and then I'm going to click on my user.

17
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Once we're here, we're going to click Impersonation Tokens, and then add a new token.

18
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:32,000
We're going to give the token a name, and we're going to set the expiration date.

19
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:39,000
I'm going to set this for February 2024, and I'm also going to give it the scope of API.

20
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:43,000
I'm then going to create the impersonation token.

21
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:48,000
You'll need to copy this token because you won't be able to see it again.

22
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
I'm just going to store it safe in my notepad.

23
00:01:52,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Once you have the impersonation token, we're going to go back into Burp, go to the cog icon, and then go to Integrations.

24
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:09,000
We're going to click Configure under GitLab, and we're going to put in the API URL for GitLab, as well as the access token.

25
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:14,000
The API URL is just the URL of your GitLab instance.

26
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
For me, it is this.

27
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Then I'm going to put in the impersonation token that I just copied before.

28
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,000
I'm then going to click Connect.

29
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:27,000
If you see this page, you know that Enterprise has successfully connected to GitLab.

30
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Now, at this point, you need to choose either Manual Issue Creation, Automatic Issue Creation, or both.

31
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:39,000
If you want to use Manual Issue Creation, then you can select the project where you want the issues to be raised.

32
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:45,000
I'm going to put this in my Project Burp project, and I'm going to choose the issue type as an issue.

33
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:51,000
If you want to allow issues to be raised in multiple projects, you can add more projects in by clicking the plus button.

34
00:02:51,000 --> 00:03:03,000
If you want to enable automatic issue creation, you can toggle the Enable section here, and select the project where you want it to be raised, and the issue type.

35
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:09,000
You can then also configure the thresholds as to when tickets should be raised, based on severity or confidence.

36
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Once you're happy with the settings, you can then click Save, and the settings will be saved.

37
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:21,000
At this point, you can go to a scan which is already completed. I've got one here.

38
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:27,000
You can find an issue which has been raised, and you can raise the GitLab issue directly from within Burp.

39
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:33,000
I'm going to create a new issue in my Project Burp project as an issue, and I'm going to click Create.

40
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:43,000
And then you can see that the ticket has been raised here, and you can click directly from Burp to go straight to the ticket which has been raised in GitLab.

41
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
And that's how you integrate GitLab and Burp Suite.

